Combat is observable: MapUnit.combatObserver (an ICombatObserver, CombatResult.cs) is told when a battle's rounds begin (MapUnit.Fight after any defensive bombard, and MapUnit.BombardUnits), who won each round or bombard shot as the engine draws it, and when the rounds are over (hit points spent, before the loser is removed or the winner promoted). The engine sends no animation messages while animations are off, so without this a headless UI cannot replay a battle round by round. The observer is called synchronously and changes nothing: no state, no draw from GameData.rng, so outcomes are as before.

